post on YouTube (<a href="https://protect.checkpoint.com/v2/r01/___https://www.youtube.com/_@LesserKnownSingapore___.YzJ1OmhzZzpjOm86MjdiMTI1ZDNiZWU5MTNkYzQ0ZDBkMjFkN2QxMzE0YzQ6NzpiNWFmOmZlM2VmMzcwNzlhOTA4YzAzZWM3NWY1ODYwZmQyOTE1YjIxMDU5NjQyYzJkZmM4ODU2YjQxY2NhNzdiMDczZDI6aDpUOkY" id="m_7954348964255817862OWA6450f515-3d2f-0df8-727c-9378bc15571b" title="Protected by Check Point: https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://www.youtube.com/@LesserKnownSingapore</a>)
 and TikTok.<br>
<br>
I have just published a post on the Changi Murals and Stanley Warren:<br>
<a href="https://protect.checkpoint.com/v2/r01/___https://pikaia.github.io/2026/10/24/the-changi-murals-stanley-warrens-chapel-paintings-at-roberts-barracks/___.YzJ1OmhzZzpjOm86MjdiMTI1ZDNiZWU5MTNkYzQ0ZDBkMjFkN2QxMzE0YzQ6NzpiZTAxOjY2ZDkzYjU1N2U0MzJiYTA3OWQ4MzE3MmE5MDk4ZWJiNWMwNTAwZWVjMWNjYWM0YzFhZjFiOTdkNmRkNjRhN2Y6aDpUOkY" id="m_7954348964255817862OWAc991a0ec-cefb-fd92-bf8b-d418d2d1f2ae" title="Protected by Check Point: https://pikaia.github.io/2026/10/24/the-changi-murals-stanley-warrens-chapel-paintings-at-roberts-barracks/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">https://pikaia.github.io/2026/10/24/the-changi-murals-stanley-warrens-chapel-paintings-at-roberts-barracks/</a><br>
<br>
The post describes the murals in words only, because I have not been able to<br>
find any freely licensed photograph of them. It points readers to the museum as<br>
the place to see the replicas. I would like to add one or two pictures of the<br>
murals, and I would be grateful for your advice on three points:<br>
<br>
1. Could the museum supply, or allow me to use, a photograph of the replica<br>
   murals on display? If it is easier, could I visit and photograph them myself<br>
   for this use?<br>
<br>
2. Does the museum or the National Heritage Board hold photographs of the<br>
   original murals in Block 151 that could be licensed, or can you tell me who<br>
   does?<br>
<br>
3. Do you know who holds the copyright in Stanley Warren&#39;s paintings today (his<br>
   family, the Ministry of Defence, or another party), so that I can ask them<br>
   too if needed?<br>
<br>
